WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:04.799
(people speaking in foreign language)

00:00:09.352 --> 00:00:13.328
(building collapsing)

00:00:13.328 --> 00:00:18.328
(pensive music)
(water whooshing)

00:00:23.346 --> 00:00:24.486
(booming sounds)

00:00:24.486 --> 00:00:25.990
(man speaking in foreign language)

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:27.600
- [Brett] Kharkiv has
been a major objective

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.940
for the Russians pretty
much from the beginning

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:30.773
of this conflict.

00:00:30.773 --> 00:00:33.480
It has seen some of the
fiercest fighting so far

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:34.330
in this war.

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:36.580
As the hours and days go by,

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:40.940
we're seeing more and more
targeting of civilian sites,

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:43.280
and we're seeing a lot
more civilian deaths

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:45.033
and casualties there.

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:47.700
(pensive music)

00:00:53.352 --> 00:00:55.971
(man speaking in foreign language)

00:00:55.971 --> 00:01:00.221
(men speaking in foreign language)

00:01:20.023 --> 00:01:23.023
(material rustling)

00:01:27.824 --> 00:01:30.491
(alarm ringing)

00:01:32.082 --> 00:01:35.915
(people talking indistinctly)

00:01:39.218 --> 00:01:42.528
(water rushing)

00:01:42.528 --> 00:01:45.195
(pensive music)

00:01:53.274 --> 00:01:57.774
(Davide speaking in foreign language)

00:01:59.276 --> 00:02:03.776
(people speaking in foreign language)

00:02:10.085 --> 00:02:12.752
(pensive music)

00:02:19.079 --> 00:02:23.829
(Volodymyr speaking in foreign language)

00:02:25.117 --> 00:02:29.867
(Volodymyr speaking in foreign language)

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:37.990
- [Brett] The Kremlin spokesman signaled

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:41.320
that Russia is indeed ready
for a second round of talks.

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:44.820
It's unclear at this point
whether those are taking place

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:47.843
and if something of substance
would really result anyway.

